Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 04:06:25 +0000
Subject: Build V8 release archives without metagen

workerd builds V8 from GitHub source archives, which do not include the
llvm-libclang and llvm-build dependencies downloaded by gclient. V8's
metagen generator needs them, so the archive cannot be built with it.

V8 15.6 enables metagen instance types by default, and V8 15.7 also
enables metagen layouts by default; both are now controlled by the
single v8_use_metagen flag. Default v8_use_metagen to False so V8 uses
the Torque-emitted instance types and the .tq object layouts, as it did
by default before 15.6.

V8 also requires the optional metagen Clang header glob to match while
loading the Bazel package, even when metagen is disabled. Allow the glob
to be empty. Builds that enable metagen still require the actual Clang
headers.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol

diff --git a/BUILD.bazel b/BUILD.bazel
index 893a49dc94102b2b13501566a029da88f25781dc..166c685a0a3cd70ca405d68847f75619b120a615 100644
--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -190,9 +190,13 @@ v8_flag(name = "v8_enable_experimental_tq_to_tsa")
 
 # Mirrors the GN arg of the same name: selects metagen's instance types and
 # object layouts. When off, the metagen action is not part of the build graph.
+#
+# Off by default for workerd: metagen needs the llvm-libclang and
+# llvm-build gclient dependencies, which are not in the V8 source
+# tarball that the workerd build fetches.
 v8_flag(
     name = "v8_use_metagen",
-    default = True,
+    default = False,
 )
 
 # Empty selects the default for the target OS. Set to "gcc" or "cl" when
@@ -4638,7 +4642,7 @@ filegroup(
     name = "metagen_clang_builtin_headers",
     srcs = glob([
         "third_party/llvm-build/Release+Asserts/lib/clang/*/include/**",
-    ]),
+    ], allow_empty = True),
 )
 
 # Metagen's checked-in C++ driver, shared with GN and metagen.py. It
